# Legacy Alembic migration history

The Alembic revisions in this directory are retained for databases created by
the former Python backend. Revisions `0001` through `0012` are historical
records and must remain available because some deployed databases may already
have applied them. `0001` through `0005` describe the pre-Rust baseline;
`0006` through `0012` are later legacy changes that are not executed by the
production Rust image.

The production Rust image does not execute Alembic. The Rust backend bootstraps
fresh databases from `sql/0001_initial.sql`, accepts databases upgraded through
the complete legacy Alembic history (ending at `0012`), and is the only
forward schema owner beginning with `rust_schema_versions` version 3. Do not
add new Alembic revisions; add future schema upgrades to both the fresh-install
SQL and the Rust upgrade path, with PostgreSQL integration coverage. A legacy
database that does not satisfy the Rust runtime signature is rejected at
startup rather than being silently stamped as compatible.
